+## Follow-up: apparent LGSSM regression
+
+The subsequent [fixed-input regression audit](ledh-lg1-regression-audit-result-2026-09-18.md) reproduced one failed LG1 case on the starting and revised implementations. Both have approximately 16.0006% maximum covariance error; their log likelihoods differ by only 3.8e-6. The actual consumer agrees. Thus the recent containment changes did not cause that replayed accuracy failure. This does not rule out regressions in other configurations or the N4096 multi-block path.
